## Key Concepts

- OpenSCAD makes 3D models by using code.
- Basic shapes can be moved, rotated, and resized.
- Variables make models easier to change.
- AI can write OpenSCAD code from a description.
- AI works better when the instructions are clear.
- AI can write correct code but still make the wrong shape.
- OpenSCAD files can be turned into STL files for 3D printing.

## What is OpenSCAD?

OpenSCAD is a program that makes 3D models with code.

Instead of dragging shapes around, you type instructions. You can make cubes, cylinders, and other shapes, then move or rotate them to build a larger model.

One useful part is that you can change a few numbers and quickly change the size of the model.

