## Real-World Applications

* OpenSCAD can be used to make parts for 3D printing.
* AI can help write the code for a model.
* Variables make it easy to make different sizes of the same object.
* Simple shapes like dice and washers worked well with AI.
* More exact objects, like brackets, were harder for AI.
* Models can be exported as STL files and prepared for a 3D printer.

